Thanks for your patience, @damienfern, and thanks @94noni for the nudge in April that nobody answered.

Everything asked for is on the head: the 6.4 leftover went to #61813, @94noni's and @alexandre-daubois' emptiness guards are in, and @OskarStark's "Available Roles" rename too. Rebased on 8.2 and pushed.

What I changed while rebasing:

 * `MermaidDumper` now sits after `$impersonateUrlGenerator` in the collector constructor, since that argument landed on 8.2 in the meantime. The three test call sites passed the dumper positionally as argument 7, so they now use `mermaidDumper:` by name and will not break again the next time an argument is added.
 * `getRolesDiagram()` returned `$this->data['roles_diagram']` for a key that is only set when a role hierarchy is configured, so calling it without one raised an undefined-key warning. It now returns null.
 * the CHANGELOG entry moved from 8.1, which has shipped, to 8.2, and the header table says 8.2.
 * squashed the four commits into one.

SecurityBundle is green at 439 tests.

@fabpot, two things for you. Your `CHANGES_REQUESTED` from 2025-09-24 appears to be a misfire: the comment attached to it is "That's a good idea indeed", agreeing with @damienfern's suggestion that Fabbot should lint CHANGELOG files, which is not a request on this PR. It has been the blocking state for eleven months, so it needs dismissing either way.

The one real decision left: this changes `MermaidDumper::dump()` to return an empty string instead of `graph TD\n    classDef default fill:#e1f5fe;` when the hierarchy is empty, so the template can skip injecting the Mermaid script. `MermaidDumper` shipped in 7.4, so that is a behaviour change on released code. It looks right to me, dumping a graph with no nodes is not useful output, and the profiler is the only consumer we ship, but it is your call rather than something to slip in.
